<!-- Blizzard, WoW Forever Beta Development Notes - Updated October 26: https://us.forums.blizzard.com/en/wow/t/2360696/7 . Only the list of changes (test data). -->
<h2><a name="p-30624529-racial-abilities-and-traits-1" class="anchor" href="#p-30624529-racial-abilities-and-traits-1" aria-label="Heading link"></a>Racial Abilities and Traits</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Human</strong>
<ul>
<li>Ruthless now increases critical chance by 1% (was 2%).</li>
<li>Human Spirit now increases Spirit by 10% (was 5%).</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Dwarf</strong>
<ul>
<li>Earth Fury (2% increased critical strike damage and healing) removed.</li>
<li>Added: Artisan’s Precision - Increases hit chance with spells and attacks by 1%.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Tauren</strong>
<ul>
<li>Plainsrunning now grants 2% movement speed per stack (was 1%), for a total max increase of 60% (was 30%).</li>
<li>Plainsrunning no longer increases mounted movement speed.</li>
<li>Endurance no longer provides any modifiers beyond 5% increased Health (no hit chance or critical damage modifiers).</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Orc</strong>
<ul>
<li>Savage removed (1% increased critical strike chance).</li>
<li>Command re-added, increasing Warlock and Hunter pet damage by 5%.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li><strong>Skyborne</strong>
<ul>
<li>Wind-Blessed Haste bonus reduced to 2% (was 3%).</li>
<li>Read Leyline now increases Mana and Health regeneration by 50% (was 100%), with a 15-second duration. This ability cannot be used while Innervate is active, and will be replaced by Innervate as a more powerful effect.</li>
<li>Using Read Leyline at a Ley Line now also grants “Attuned” for 1 hour. While Attuned, the benefit of Read Leyline is increased to 100% regeneration increase. Attuned persists through death.</li>
<li>Skysight is now a 15% increased movement speed (was 10%), with a 15-second duration.</li>
<li>Using Skysight at an elemental convergence now also grants “Charged” for 1 hour. While Charged, the benefit of Skysight is a 30% movement speed increase. Charged persists through death.</li>
</ul>
</li>
</ul>
